      "text": "LLD PATTERN GUIDE — WHICH ONE SHOULD I USE?",
      "fontSize": 31,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 28,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "LLD PATTERN GUIDE — WHICH ONE SHOULD I USE?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "a0"
    },
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 62,
      "y": 105,
      "width": 1420,
      "height": 80,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#343a40",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 302,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791480000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Start with the problem you have. These patterns solve different problems; they are not competing ways to do the same thing.\nFolders: Creational = how objects are made; Behavioral = how objects collaborate or vary behavior; Structural = how objects/classes are composed.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 17,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Start with the problem you have. These patterns solve different problems; they are not competing ways to do the same thing.\nFolders: Creational = how objects are made; Behavioral = how objects collaborate or vary behavior; Structural = how objects/classes are composed.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "a1"
    },
    {
